      "message": "feat(post): Fanuc rigid tap option writes M29 S before G84\n\nA new Fanuc post option, rigidTapM29 (off by default), writes\nM29 S<rpm> on the block right before each G84 block that opens a cycle\ngroup. G80 ends rigid mode, so each group states it again. A section\nwith no spindle speed is refused by name, not posted with M29 S0.\n\nOff by default keeps every golden unchanged: a control with parameter\n5200 bit 0 set taps rigid on G84 alone.\n\nRefs #2603\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
